  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Gradual warming and dry weather will persist through \nSaturday, then chances for rain enters Sunday with a period of dry \nweather to return for the start of the new work week.\n\nCoastal low pressure maturing off the New England coast today and \ninto the weekend will result in surface high pressure centered over \neastern Canada to continue to settle south across the region \ntonight, before pushing westward across the central Great Lakes by \nSaturday. Overall this will promote fair weather into the start of \nthe weekend. \n\nThe aforementioned coastal low will progress towards Cape Cod \nSaturday night, which will support its cloud shield to spread \nwestward across the region. This low will jut westward toward New \nJersey Sunday while weakening, which will cause the precipitation \nshield to spread westward across the eastern portions of the \nforecast area, mainly impacting areas east of the Genesee Valley. \nHowever, the westward trend of the coastal low's track may introduce \na few light rain showers to filter further west across Western New \nYork Sunday.\n\nSurface high pressure will return to the eastern Great Lakes and \nOhio Valley early next week, supporting dry weather to return.",
